      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/aplocheilichthys-normani-2/",
      "html": "<p>Aplocheilichthys normani (= Poropanchax normani) is a classic among the fish species that Takashi Amano preferred to use for his nature aquarium setups.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/aplocheilichthys-normani-2/",
      "html": "<p>A single specimen of this lampeye is a rather drab creature, but a larger school in a tank with dimmed light is like magic! The blue eyes drift like small fireflies through the underwater world.</p><p>Both wild-caught fish from Guinea and bred fish from Indonesia are available. Keeping these fish is very easy, but avoid the mistake of keeping too few specimens. A school of 20-30 animals is perfect.</p>"
